{"id":"anti-pattern-rl-001","type":"anti-pattern","fact":"Dead variable left after code path removal: removing a code path that is the sole consumer of a variable leaves the variable as dead code. In WU-RL2, removing the 3-pass scalar fallback left use_avx2_tanh dead (it was only passed to bulk_tanh_dispatched which was removed). Dead variables cause compiler warnings and are misleading to reviewers.","recommendation":"When removing a code path, explicitly audit for variables whose only use was inside that path. Remove the variable declarations at the same time. Check both the deleted path AND the dispatch check that enabled it.","confidence":"high","provenance":["WU-RL2 use_avx2_tanh cleanup"],"tags":["cpp","dead-code","cleanup","robloc"],"affectedFiles":["src/rob_loc.cpp"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-03-24","updatedAt":"2026-03-24","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
